# Metadata Viewer — Admin assets

- Scripts are registered in `includes/Assets.php` with handles like `metadata_viewer_admin_script` and `metadata_viewer_highlight_script`; enqueue dependencies (`jquery` where needed) and use `METADATA_VIEWER_PLUGIN_VERSION` for cache busting.
- Keep admin JS compatible with jQuery usage already on edit screens; avoid breaking the metadata filter/search UI wired in `assets/admin/js/script.js`.
- CSS lives under `assets/admin/css/`; align class names with templates in `templates/` (e.g. `.metadata-viewer-wrapper`, `.metadata-viewer-table`).
- `phpcs.xml` excludes `assets/` from PHP scanning — still follow sensible front-end hygiene (no inline secrets, minimal global pollution).
